module

public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IntermediateField.Adjoin.Algebra
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Henselian
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.EppUnramifiedBaseChange
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Embedding the finite unramified base change of Epp's route into `B`

`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.EppUnramifiedBaseChange` constructs, from Epp's
residue-field condition, a finite weakly unramified extension `A₁ / A` of discrete valuation rings
whose residue field is `κ_A`-isomorphic to `perfectCore κ_B p`.  That is only half of what the
route needs: to *use* the base change one must replace the pair `(A, B)` by `(A₁, B)`, and for that
`A₁` has to sit inside `B` over `A`.

This file supplies the embedding, and it is Hensel's lemma that supplies it.  The extension is
`A₁ = A[X] ⧸ (P)` for a monic `P ∈ A[X]` lifting `minpoly κ_A α`, where `α` is a primitive element
of the perfect core; so an `A`-algebra map `A₁ → B` is *exactly* a root of `P` in `B`.  The
reduction `P̄ = minpoly κ_A α` has the root `α` in `κ_B` — the perfect core is a subfield of `κ_B`
— and that root is **simple**, because `minpoly κ_A α` is separable, which is precisely Epp's
condition (`Stacks.EppTheorem.EppCondition.isSeparable_perfectCore`).  A simple root of the residue
reduction lifts to a root in `B` as soon as `B` is henselian.

## The henselian hypothesis

The statement of Tag 09F9 formalised in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.EppUnramifiedBaseChange` carries no completeness or
henselian hypothesis on `B`, and none is needed there: the base change is built out of `A` alone.
The embedding is different.  Lifting a root of `P̄` from `κ_B` to `B` is exactly the henselian
property of `B`, and it genuinely fails for a general discrete valuation ring — a non-henselian
`B` has, by definition, a monic polynomial with a simple residue root that lifts to no root.  So
every result below that produces a map into `B` carries `[HenselianLocalRing B]`.  In Epp's
argument this is free: the proof of 09F9 replaces `A → B` by the extension of the *completions*
first (`Stacks.EppTheorem.EppCondition.of_residueField_surjective` is the transfer of Epp's
  condition
along that replacement), and a complete discrete valuation ring is henselian via Mathlib's
`IsAdicComplete.henselianRing`.

## Main results

* `AdjoinRoot.adjoin_residue_root_eq_top`: the residue field of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` is generated over
  `κ_A` by the residue of the adjoined root.
* `AdjoinRoot.exists_algHom_residue_root_eq_of_henselian`: **layer (1), Hensel's lemma as an
  embedding statement.**  For `P` monic over a local ring `A`, a local homomorphism `A → B` with
  `B` henselian local, and a *simple* root `x ∈ κ_B` of the residue reduction `P̄`, there is an
  `A`-algebra map `A[X] ⧸ (P) → B` carrying the adjoined root to a lift of `x`.  The conclusion
  pins the image of the root, so the map cannot be a degenerate one that ignores `x`.
* `AdjoinRoot.isLocalHom_of_algHom`: any `A`-algebra map out of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` into a local ring is
  automatically a local homomorphism, `P̄` being irreducible — the maximal ideal upstairs is
  generated by the image of a uniformizer of `A`.
* `Stacks.EppTheorem.exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_of_isSeparable`: **layers
  (2) and
  (3), for an arbitrary finite separable residue extension `E`.**  The base change realising `E`
  embeds into `B` over `A`, and its residue field is carried *onto* `E`:
  `(algebraMap κ_{A₁} κ_B).fieldRange = E`.  Stated for a general `E` because the two cases the
  route needs are different: `E = perfectCore κ_B p` gives the equality invariant below but costs
  finiteness of the perfect core, while `E` generated by a finite subset of the perfect core costs
  nothing and is what `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.EppFiniteSupport` uses.
* `Stacks.EppTheorem.exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_perfectCore`: **layers (2)
  and
  (3).**  Under Epp's condition, finite-dimensionality of the perfect core and henselianness of
  `B`, the finite weakly unramified base change `A₁ / A` can be produced *together with* an
  `A`-algebra structure map `A₁ → B` making `A → A₁ → B` a tower of local homomorphisms, and then
  the residue field of `A₁` is carried **onto** the perfect core of `κ_B`:
  `(algebraMap κ_{A₁} κ_B).fieldRange = perfectCore κ_B p`.  This is the equality invariant that
  Tag 09F8 consumes.

## References

* [Epp, *Elimination of wild ramification*][epp1973]
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 09F9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09F9)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 09F8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09F8)
-/

@[expose] public section

open IsLocalRing Polynomial

namespace AdjoinRoot

/-! ### The residue field of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` is monogenic -/

section AdjoinResidueRoot

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] {P : A[X]} [IsLocalRing (AdjoinRoot P)]
  [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A (AdjoinRoot P))]

/-- **The residue field of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` is generated by the residue of the adjoined root.**

Every element of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` is `mk P g` for some `g ∈ A[X]`, and its residue is the value of the
reduction `ḡ ∈ κ_A[X]` at the residue of the adjoined root; so the residues of the adjoined root
generate the residue field as a `κ_A`-algebra.

This is the form of the identification of the residue field that the range computation in
`Stacks.EppTheorem.exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_perfectCore` needs.  It is a
statement about the residue of the root itself, rather than about the abstract isomorphism
`AdjoinRoot.residueFieldAlgEquiv`, which is what makes it usable: the isomorphism there is built
by `AlgEquiv.ofBijective` and carries no equation for the image of the root. -/
theorem adjoin_residue_root_eq_top :
    Algebra.adjoin (ResidueField A)
      ({residue (AdjoinRoot P) (AdjoinRoot.root P)} : Set (ResidueField (AdjoinRoot P))) = ⊤ := by
  have hcomp : (algebraMap (ResidueField A) (ResidueField (AdjoinRoot P))).comp (residue A) =
      (residue (AdjoinRoot P)).comp (algebraMap A (AdjoinRoot P)) := RingHom.ext fun _ => rfl
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun z _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := residue_surjective (R := AdjoinRoot P) z
  induction y using AdjoinRoot.induction_on with
  | ih g =>
    rw [Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval, AlgHom.mem_range]
    refine ⟨g.map (residue A), ?_⟩
    rw [aeval_def, eval₂_map, hcomp, ← hom_eval₂, ← aeval_def, AdjoinRoot.aeval_eq]

end AdjoinResidueRoot

/-! ### Layer (1): Hensel's lemma as an embedding statement -/

/-- **A simple root of the residue reduction gives an `A`-algebra map `A[X] ⧸ (P) → B`.**

Let `A → B` be a local homomorphism of local rings with `B` henselian, let `P ∈ A[X]` be monic,
and let `x ∈ κ_B` be a root of the reduction `P̄ ∈ κ_A[X]` (read in `κ_B` through
`κ_A → κ_B`) which is **simple**, i.e. the derivative of `P̄` does not vanish at `x`.  Then there
is an `A`-algebra homomorphism `A[X] ⧸ (P) → B` sending the adjoined root to an element of `B`
with residue `x`.

Since an `A`-algebra map out of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` is the same thing as a root of `P` in `B`, this is
exactly Hensel's lemma; the henselian property enters through clause (2) of
`HenselianLocalRing.TFAE`, the residue-field form of root lifting.

The conclusion records where the adjoined root goes.  Without that clause the statement would be
discharged by any map at all, and in the intended application it is the *choice* of the root `x`
that determines the image of the residue field, so the clause is the content. -/
theorem exists_algHom_residue_root_eq_of_henselian {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [IsLocalRing A] [HenselianLocalRing B] [Algebra A B] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)] {P : A[X]}
    (hP : P.Monic) {x : ResidueField B} (hroot : aeval x (P.map (residue A)) = 0)
    (hsimple : aeval x (derivative (P.map (residue A))) ≠ 0) :
    ∃ φ : AdjoinRoot P →ₐ[A] B, residue B (φ (AdjoinRoot.root P)) = x := by
  have hcomp : (algebraMap (ResidueField A) (ResidueField B)).comp (residue A) =
      (residue B).comp (algebraMap A B) := RingHom.ext fun _ => rfl
  have key : ∀ q : A[X], aeval x (q.map (residue A)) = aeval x (q.map (algebraMap A B)) := by
    intro q
    rw [aeval_def, eval₂_map, hcomp, aeval_def, eval₂_map,
      IsLocalRing.ResidueField.algebraMap_eq]
  have h1 : aeval x (P.map (algebraMap A B)) = 0 := by rwa [← key]
  have h2 : aeval x (derivative (P.map (algebraMap A B))) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [derivative_map] at hsimple ⊢
    rwa [← key]
  have hB : ∀ f : B[X], f.Monic → ∀ a₀ : ResidueField B, aeval a₀ f = 0 →
      aeval a₀ (derivative f) ≠ 0 → ∃ a : B, f.IsRoot a ∧ residue B a = a₀ :=
    ((HenselianLocalRing.TFAE B).out 1 2).mp ‹HenselianLocalRing B›
  obtain ⟨a, haroot, hares⟩ := hB _ (hP.map _) x h1 h2
  have heval : P.eval₂ ((Algebra.ofId A B : A →ₐ[A] B) : A →+* B) a = 0 := by
    rw [← eval_map]
    exact haroot
  refine ⟨AdjoinRoot.liftAlgHom P (Algebra.ofId A B) a heval, ?_⟩
  rw [AdjoinRoot.liftAlgHom_root]
  exact hares

/-! ### Any `A`-algebra map out of the unramified extension is local -/

/-- **An `A`-algebra map out of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` into a local ring is a local homomorphism.**

When `P̄` is irreducible the maximal ideal of `A[X] ⧸ (P)` is generated by the image of a
uniformizer `π` of `A` (`AdjoinRoot.maximalIdeal_eq_span_algebraMap`), so a nonunit upstairs is
`π` times something; an `A`-algebra map sends it into the ideal generated by the image of `π` in
`B`, which is a nonunit because `A → B` is local.

This is what upgrades the embedding of `AdjoinRoot.exists_algHom_residue_root_eq_of_henselian` to
a map of *local* rings, hence to a map of residue fields. -/
theorem isLocalHom_of_algHom {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra A B] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)] {P : A[X]}
    [IsLocalRing (AdjoinRoot P)] (hirr : Irreducible (P.map (residue A)))
    (ψ : AdjoinRoot P →ₐ[A] B) : IsLocalHom (ψ : AdjoinRoot P →+* B) := by
  obtain ⟨π, hπ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible A
  refine ⟨fun a ha => ?_⟩
  by_contra hna
  have hmem : a ∈ maximalIdeal (AdjoinRoot P) := by
    rwa [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal, mem_nonunits_iff]
  rw [AdjoinRoot.maximalIdeal_eq_span_algebraMap hirr hπ, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hmem
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hmem
  have hψπ : (ψ : AdjoinRoot P →+* B) (algebraMap A (AdjoinRoot P) π) = algebraMap A B π :=
    ψ.commutes π
  rw [map_mul, hψπ] at ha
  exact hπ.not_isUnit (isUnit_of_map_unit (algebraMap A B) π (isUnit_of_mul_isUnit_left ha))

end AdjoinRoot

/-! ### Layers (2) and (3): the base change embeds, and carries the perfect core -/

namespace Stacks.EppTheorem

universe u v

/-- If `x` generates `S` as an `R`-algebra, every element of `S` is a polynomial in `x`. -/
private theorem exists_aeval_eq_of_adjoin_eq_top {R S : Type*} [CommSemiring R] [Semiring S]
    [Algebra R S] {x : S} (h : Algebra.adjoin R {x} = ⊤) (z : S) : ∃ g : R[X], aeval x g = z := by
  rw [← AlgHom.mem_range, ← Algebra.adjoin_singleton_eq_range_aeval, h]
  exact Algebra.mem_top

/-- **The finite unramified base change at a finite separable residue extension embeds into `B`,
and its residue field is carried onto that extension.**

Let `A → B` be a local homomorphism of discrete valuation rings with `B` henselian, and let `E` be
an intermediate field of `κ_B / κ_A` which is finite and separable over `κ_A`.  Then there is a
discrete valuation ring `A₁`, finite and weakly unramified over `A`, carrying an algebra structure
map `A₁ → B` making `A → A₁ → B` a tower of local homomorphisms, and for that embedding

`(algebraMap κ_{A₁} κ_B).fieldRange = E`.

The construction is the monogenic one: a primitive element `α` of `E / κ_A`, its minimal polynomial
`q`, a monic lift `P ∈ A[X]` of `q`, and `A₁ = A[X] ⧸ (P)`.  What makes the *embedding* available
is that `α` already lies in `κ_B` and is a **simple** root of `q` there — simple because `q` is
separable — so Hensel's lemma over the henselian `B` lifts it to an `A`-algebra map.  The clause of
`AdjoinRoot.exists_algHom_residue_root_eq_of_henselian` pinning the image of the adjoined root is
what makes the range come out *equal* to `E` rather than merely contained in it; without it the
statement would be discharged by a degenerate map and would carry no absorption information.

This is the general form.  `exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_perfectCore` is the
instance `E = perfectCore κ_B p`, which needs the perfect core to be finite over `κ_A`;
`Stacks.EppTheorem.EppCondition.exists_isWeaklyUnramified_absorbing_finset` is the instance where
  `E` is
generated by a *finite subset* of the perfect core, and that one needs no finiteness hypothesis on
the perfect core at all. -/
@[sga "3 V 4.1.2" "special case", sga "7 XXII 4.4" "more general"]
theorem exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_of_isSeparable {A : Type u} {B : Type v}
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing B] [HenselianLocalRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
    (E : IntermediateField (ResidueField A) (ResidueField B))
    [Algebra.IsSeparable (ResidueField A) E] [FiniteDimensional (ResidueField A) E] :
    ∃ (A₁ : Type u) (_ : CommRing A₁) (_ : IsDomain A₁) (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing A₁)
      (_ : Algebra A A₁) (_ : Module.Finite A A₁)
      (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing.IsExtension A A₁) (_ : Algebra A₁ B)
      (_ : IsScalarTower A A₁ B) (_ : IsLocalHom (algebraMap A₁ B)),
      IsDiscreteValuationRing.IsWeaklyUnramified A A₁ ∧
        Nonempty (ResidueField A₁ ≃ₐ[ResidueField A] E) ∧
        (algebraMap (ResidueField A₁) (ResidueField B)).fieldRange = E.toSubfield := by
  obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := Field.exists_primitive_element (ResidueField A) E
  have hint : IsIntegral (ResidueField A) α := IsIntegral.of_finite (ResidueField A) α
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hPmap⟩ := exists_monic_lift_map_residue_eq A (minpoly.monic hint)
  have hirr : Irreducible (P.map (residue A)) := hPmap ▸ minpoly.irreducible hint
  have hd : 0 < P.natDegree := by
    rw [← hP.natDegree_map (residue A), hPmap]
    exact minpoly.natDegree_pos hint
  have haeval : aeval ((α : ResidueField B)) (minpoly (ResidueField A) α) = 0 := by
    rw [show ((α : ResidueField B)) = E.val α from rfl, aeval_algHom_apply, minpoly.aeval,
      map_zero]
  have hsimple : aeval ((α : ResidueField B)) (derivative (minpoly (ResidueField A) α)) ≠ 0 :=
    (Algebra.IsSeparable.isSeparable (ResidueField A) α).aeval_derivative_ne_zero haeval
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψ⟩ := AdjoinRoot.exists_algHom_residue_root_eq_of_henselian hP
    (x := (α : ResidueField B)) (by rwa [hPmap]) (by rwa [hPmap])
  have hdeg : 0 < P.degree := Polynomial.natDegree_pos_iff_degree_pos.mp hd
  have hlocal := AdjoinRoot.isLocalRing_of_irreducible_map_residue hP hirr
  have hdom := AdjoinRoot.isDomain_of_irreducible_map_residue hP hirr
  have hlh := AdjoinRoot.isLocalHom_of_monic_of_degree_pos (g := P) hP hdeg
  have hdvr := AdjoinRoot.isDiscreteValuationRing hP hirr hd
  have hext : IsDiscreteValuationRing.IsExtension A (AdjoinRoot P) :=
    { toFaithfulSMul := AdjoinRoot.faithfulSMul_of_monic_of_degree_pos hP hdeg,
      toIsLocalHom := hlh }
  let algψ : Algebra (AdjoinRoot P) B := (ψ : AdjoinRoot P →+* B).toAlgebra
  have hamap : (algebraMap (AdjoinRoot P) B) = (ψ : AdjoinRoot P →+* B) := rfl
  have htower : IsScalarTower A (AdjoinRoot P) B :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x => (ψ.commutes x).symm
  have hlhψ : IsLocalHom (algebraMap (AdjoinRoot P) B) :=
    hamap ▸ AdjoinRoot.isLocalHom_of_algHom hirr ψ
  have hroot_res : algebraMap (ResidueField (AdjoinRoot P)) (ResidueField B)
      (residue (AdjoinRoot P) (AdjoinRoot.root P)) = E.val α := by
    rw [IsLocalRing.ResidueField.algebraMap_residue, hamap]
    exact hψ
  have htopE : Algebra.adjoin (ResidueField A) ({α} : Set E) = ⊤ := by
    have h := IntermediateField.adjoin_simple_toSubalgebra_of_isAlgebraic
      (F := ResidueField A) (α := α) hint.isAlgebraic
    rw [hα, IntermediateField.top_toSubalgebra] at h
    exact h.symm
  have hfr : (algebraMap (ResidueField (AdjoinRoot P)) (ResidueField B)).fieldRange =
      E.toSubfield := by
    have hcalc : ∀ g : (ResidueField A)[X],
        algebraMap (ResidueField (AdjoinRoot P)) (ResidueField B)
            (aeval (residue (AdjoinRoot P) (AdjoinRoot.root P)) g) = E.val (aeval α g) := by
      intro g
      rw [← aeval_algebraMap_apply (ResidueField B), hroot_res, aeval_algHom_apply]
    refine le_antisymm (fun y hy => ?_) fun y hy => ?_
    · obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := RingHom.mem_fieldRange.mp hy
      obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := exists_aeval_eq_of_adjoin_eq_top
        (AdjoinRoot.adjoin_residue_root_eq_top (P := P)) z
      rw [hcalc g, IntermediateField.mem_toSubfield]
      exact (aeval α g).2
    · obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := exists_aeval_eq_of_adjoin_eq_top htopE
        (⟨y, (IntermediateField.mem_toSubfield E y).mp hy⟩ : E)
      exact RingHom.mem_fieldRange.mpr
        ⟨aeval (residue (AdjoinRoot P) (AdjoinRoot.root P)) g, by rw [hcalc g, hg]; rfl⟩
  refine ⟨AdjoinRoot P, inferInstance, hdom, hdvr, inferInstance, hP.finite_adjoinRoot, hext, algψ,
    htower, hlhψ, AdjoinRoot.ramificationIdx_eq_one hP hirr hd,
    ⟨(AdjoinRoot.residueFieldAlgEquiv hP hirr hd).symm.trans
      ((AdjoinRoot.algEquivOfEq (ResidueField A) _ _ hPmap).trans
        (AdjoinRoot.algEquivOfPrimitiveElement hint hα))⟩,
    hfr⟩

/-- **The finite unramified base change of Epp's route embeds into `B`, and its residue field is
carried onto the perfect core.**

Let `A → B` be a local homomorphism of discrete valuation rings with `κ_A` perfect of exponential
characteristic `p`, and assume

* `B` is henselian (see the module docstring: this is what root lifting costs, and it is free
  after passing to completions);
* Epp's condition: every element of `perfectCore κ_B p` is separable algebraic over `κ_A`;
* `perfectCore κ_B p` is finite-dimensional over `κ_A`.

Then the finite weakly unramified extension `A₁ / A` produced by
`Stacks.EppTheorem.exists_isWeaklyUnramified_residueField_algEquiv_perfectCore` can be produced
  together
with an `A₁`-algebra structure on `B` making `A → A₁ → B` a tower of local homomorphisms, and for
that embedding

`(algebraMap κ_{A₁} κ_B).fieldRange = perfectCore κ_B p`.

That equality is the invariant Tag 09F8 wants — the image of the base residue field in `κ_B` is
*exactly* the perfect core — and the point of the whole base change is to arrange it.  One
inclusion is Epp's condition together with perfectness of `κ_A`, and the other is the fact that
the residue field of `A₁` realises a primitive element of the perfect core; both come out of
`AdjoinRoot.adjoin_residue_root_eq_top` once the embedding is known to send the adjoined root to
that primitive element, which is the clause carried by
`AdjoinRoot.exists_algHom_residue_root_eq_of_henselian`.

The `Nonempty (ResidueField A₁ ≃ₐ[κ_A] perfectCore …)` clause is retained from the base change
itself, so this statement subsumes the earlier one except for the henselian hypothesis. -/
theorem exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_perfectCore {A : Type u} {B : Type v}
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing B] [HenselianLocalRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)] (p : ℕ) [ExpChar (ResidueField A) p]
    [ExpChar (ResidueField B) p] [PerfectField (ResidueField A)] (hepp : EppCondition A B p)
    (hfin : FiniteDimensional (ResidueField A)
      (perfectCoreIntermediateField (ResidueField A) (ResidueField B) p)) :
    ∃ (A₁ : Type u) (_ : CommRing A₁) (_ : IsDomain A₁) (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing A₁)
      (_ : Algebra A A₁) (_ : Module.Finite A A₁)
      (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing.IsExtension A A₁) (_ : Algebra A₁ B)
      (_ : IsScalarTower A A₁ B) (_ : IsLocalHom (algebraMap A₁ B)),
      IsDiscreteValuationRing.IsWeaklyUnramified A A₁ ∧
        Nonempty (ResidueField A₁ ≃ₐ[ResidueField A]
          perfectCoreIntermediateField (ResidueField A) (ResidueField B) p) ∧
        (algebraMap (ResidueField A₁) (ResidueField B)).fieldRange =
          perfectCore (ResidueField B) p := by
  have := hfin
  have := hepp.isSeparable_perfectCore
  obtain ⟨A₁, _, hdom, hdvr, _, hmf, hext, algψ, htower, hlhψ, hwu, hequiv, hfr⟩ :=
    exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_of_isSeparable (A := A) (B := B)
      (perfectCoreIntermediateField (ResidueField A) (ResidueField B) p)
  refine ⟨A₁, inferInstance, hdom, hdvr, inferInstance, hmf, hext, algψ, htower, hlhψ, hwu,
    hequiv, ?_⟩
  rw [hfr]
  exact Subfield.ext fun x =>
    (IntermediateField.mem_toSubfield _ x).trans mem_perfectCoreIntermediateField_iff

/-- **Layer (2) in isolation: the base change admits an `A`-algebra map to `B`.**

The `A`-algebra homomorphism is the structure map of the tower produced by
`Stacks.EppTheorem.exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_perfectCore`; this is the
  form in
which "replace `(A, B)` by `(A₁, B)`" is usually quoted. -/
theorem exists_isWeaklyUnramified_nonempty_algHom {A : Type u} {B : Type v} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsDomain A] [IsDomain B] [IsDiscreteValuationRing A]
    [IsDiscreteValuationRing B] [HenselianLocalRing B] [Algebra A B]
    [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)] (p : ℕ) [ExpChar (ResidueField A) p]
    [ExpChar (ResidueField B) p] [PerfectField (ResidueField A)] (hepp : EppCondition A B p)
    (hfin : FiniteDimensional (ResidueField A)
      (perfectCoreIntermediateField (ResidueField A) (ResidueField B) p)) :
    ∃ (A₁ : Type u) (_ : CommRing A₁) (_ : IsDomain A₁) (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing A₁)
      (_ : Algebra A A₁) (_ : Module.Finite A A₁)
      (_ : IsDiscreteValuationRing.IsExtension A A₁),
      IsDiscreteValuationRing.IsWeaklyUnramified A A₁ ∧ Nonempty (A₁ →ₐ[A] B) := by
  obtain ⟨A₁, _, _, _, _, hmf, hext, _, htower, _, hwu, -, -⟩ :=
    exists_isWeaklyUnramified_algebraMap_fieldRange_eq_perfectCore (A := A) (B := B) p hepp hfin
  exact ⟨A₁, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, inferInstance, hmf, hext, hwu,
    ⟨IsScalarTower.toAlgHom A A₁ B⟩⟩

end Stacks.EppTheorem
